tiply rather than copying the worked model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Common error: Skipping inverse checks on review hides quotient errors. Correction: Multiplication structure / partial products; factors. Why: the correction restores accurate use of review.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Skipping inverse checks on review hides quotient errors. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Solve one fresh problem that uses review with different numbers from the worked model. Show working and name the places or values that matter.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Describe one likely mistake with review, show corrected working, and say why the correction works.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Require new numbers, visible working and named places/values. / Require a real misconception, corrected working and a method reason..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Multiplication structure / partial products; factors. This matches the lesson skill for review.","options":["Ignore place value and read digits from left to right as ones only.","Copy the model numbers and call that independent work.","Multiplication structure / partial products; factors.","Skipping inverse checks on review hides quotient errors."],"question":"Name two skills: area model for 24×6; factors of 16. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Skipping inverse checks on review hides quotient errors. That misconception weakens accuracy; the other choices align with the lesson idea.","options":["Skipping inverse checks on review hides quotient errors.","Unit review mixes facts, written multiply/divide, remainders, word problems and factors/multiples with inverse checks.","Multiplication structure / partial products; factors.","Careful use of multiply with clear evidence."],"question":"Which statement is a 